caption: Covenant Failure
setting-component: covenant-failure

If the quota is not met by dawn, Niktul does not necessarily attack France directly. He simply stops protecting it.

The suppressed supernatural conditions return toward their natural values. SPA rises. Mana rises, potentially to High or Very High. Spontaneous Gates can open. Monsters that had been repelled can enter. Existing supernatural threats become much more dangerous under the restored SPA conditions.

France then endures the remainder of the lunar month as ordinary GATES Earth.

At the next Blood Moon, France faces the same choice again: provide Niktul with the required sacrifices and restore the protection, or continue living without the Covenant.

This history makes the Blood Moon politically durable. Covenant failure is not an abstract theological threat. France can have recorded historical failures, survivors, ruined communities, and institutional contingency plans demonstrating what happens when the country refuses or cannot pay Niktul’s price.
